    }
  ],
  "technical_issues": [
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "At 600 km altitude, a sun-synchronous orbit requires a retrograde inclination of approximately 97.8°, not 87.79°. The stated inclination is prograde and would not produce the claimed sun-synchronous nodal precession; the plotted curve itself is near 97.8° at 600 km."
    },
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "The semi-major axis is inconsistent with the stated Earth radius and altitude: 6371 km + 600 km = 6971 km, not 7171 km."
    },
    {
      "where": "Launch",
      "issue": "Kourou is near 5.2° N, not 45.05° N. This also invalidates the stated comparison of the launch-site latitude with the target inclination."
    },
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "RAAN is not determined by the launch facility's location as stated; it is an inertial orbital orientation that depends on launch timing and epoch."
    },
    {
      "where": "Ground Control & Communications",
      "issue": "The reported mean access duration of 580.786 seconds is about 9.7 minutes, not almost twenty minutes."
    },
    {
      "where": "Ground Control & Communications",
      "issue": "The report assumes Mount Pleasant Radio Observatory can provide spacecraft communications without establishing suitable TT&C antennas, frequencies, or link performance. A sun-synchronous orbit also does not guarantee continuous sunlight or a daylight descending track; local solar time and eclipse conditions are not specified."
    }
  ],
  "overall": "A clearly structured concept with useful STK visualisations and coverage of the requested mission segments. The central orbit has substantial calculation and interpretation errors, while operator/customer roles, ground-station capability, and supporting software files are incomplete. The design therefore needs significant technical correction before it can support its stated mission objectives."
}
